# Uniform propagation estimates for closed finite-chain shoulders

`exists_uniform_physicalDirectRelation_closed_shoulders` constructs a positive
width, common compact base carrier and frequency annulus before the varying
coefficient field. Every closed shoulder through the fixed depth is in
`physicalProtectedRegion`, and the initial shoulder stays in its source buffer.
The width may be decreased without changing any bound.

`exists_initialized_signed_no_return_with_closed_shoulders` instantiates the
coefficient budget, retained comparison jets, angular margin and source cover
on the SAME initialized witnesses, preserving every original conclusion.
`GraphShoulders` includes the initially elliptic and all-diagonal cases;
`SourceNeighborhood` constructs robustness from the fixed product buffers.
`Recutting` transfers the result to the original source restriction over
`tsupport χ₂`, where `sourceRecutRelation_outer_eq_one` supplies `χ₃ = 1`.

The finite root selector remains with the arbitrary-accuracy parent. Its inputs
here are the literal compact restrictions of the primitive root/flow buffers,
not assumptions about any propagated shoulder or successful mask.

Consumer: the nested-mask assembly in `ProtectedMasks.Uniformity`, for the
protected finite-chain paragraph of `app:ch_regular:lem:finite-chain`.
-/
